# Authentication is handled by the FastAPI backend (email/password + Google
# Sign-In + session cookie — see geo_pipeline/auth.py, geo_pipeline/google_auth.py).
# The /api/auth/* routes only need NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL (see .env.example) to
# reach that backend.
#
# There is no Clerk and no MySQL/Postgres in this build. Login data lives in
# geo_pipeline/data/app.db (SQLite, created automatically, gitignored).

# Google Sign-In (Google Identity Services). Public by design — this is the
# OAuth Web Client ID, not a secret; it must match the backend's own
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID (geo_pipeline/.env) exactly, since FastAPI checks every ID
# token's `aud` claim against its value. Leave blank to disable Google
# Sign-In entirely — GoogleSignInButton then renders nothing and email/
# password auth is unaffected.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
